    "description": {
      "value": "<p>At 11th level, you can release your power to control the winds around you on a powerful tornado. As an Action, the air swirl around you in a fast speed, forming a cylinder 20-foot wide and 30-foot high around you. All creatures in the area need to succeed on a Dexterity saving throw, taking 4d6 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half as much on a success. In addition, any creature in the area needs to also make a Strength saving throw or be pushed back to the edge of the area of effect.</p><p>The damage increases to 6d6 at 17th level.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
